From 26f51dae6bcfc4aa872f8cbc8e646e9d4fffce5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:52:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/51] B70-IP-PAD16: D2 split views and K4 dequant follow the
 16-B padded per-token-head slot

FLASH_ATTN's D2 spec already delegates to TritonAttentionBackend.customize_spec,
so D2 pages stay byte-identical to TRITON_ATTN / QSA pages (544 B per slot at
hs 256; hybrid unify and K3 unchanged). split_layout_views now accepts the
spec's content width (pth_half_ok: tight or 16-B padded) instead of exactly
2 * (D + 4); the kernel's block-local split layout [int8 K|V | K scales |
V scales] uses the first H*N*(2D+8) bytes of each page and leaves the rest
unused, all surfaces still 64-B aligned (page = N*H*544 is a 64-B multiple
whenever N*H is even). K4 dequant reads [:hs] of any half (comment only).

Tests (CPU, Triton interpreter; every test on both layouts): spec 544/520 ==
TRITON_ATTN, split views == kernel reference views, wrong content refused,
writer round trip through the split views, K4 parity inline vs split,
fa_int8_forward routing vs an fp32 reference.
